# Turtle-Duck: "base power 4" is a layer 7b setting effect that sets only the power (CR 613.4b), and a later one overrides an earlier
# one by timestamp. Quandrix Charm first makes the 0/4 Duck a 5/5; the ability then sets base power 4 only, so it is a 4/5 with trample
# (toughness 5 is kept, and the power is 4 and not 5+4).

[Bot1 Deck]
Turtle-Duck
Quandrix Charm
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Island x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald#1.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Turtle-Duck.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Quandrix Charm.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Target creature has base power and toughness 5/5)
Bot1.Target(Turtle-Duck)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Turtle-Duck.Power = 5
? Bot1.Battlefield.Turtle-Duck.Toughness = 5
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Turtle-Duck.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Turtle-Duck.Power = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Turtle-Duck.Toughness = 5
Bot1.Battlefield.Turtle-Duck.Keywords = Trample
